\subsubsection*{Breast Cancer Gene Panel}
The 24‑gene panel used for encoding and coherence analysis incorporated the most frequently altered pathways identified in TCGA‑BRCA datasets.  

\subsection{Molecular Subtype Profiles (TCGA‑BRCA Derived)}

Subtype configurations were generated according to published mutation frequencies and receptor status. Coherence (NRCI) values were computed for each:

\begin{itemize}[leftmargin=1.2em]
  \item \textbf{Healthy Baseline:} All 24 genes = 0 (\( \mathrm{NRCI} = 1.0000 \))
  \item \textbf{Luminal A (ER+/PR+/HER2–):} 4 dysregulations (17 \%)  
    PIK3CA, GATA3, CDH1, MAP3K1; \( \mathrm{NRCI} = 0.8333 \)
  \item \textbf{Luminal B (ER+/PR+/HER2+):} 7 dysregulations (29 \%)  
    PIK3CA, GATA3, CDH1, MAP3K1, TP53, ERBB2, CCND1; \( \mathrm{NRCI} = 0.7083 \)
  \item \textbf{HER2‑Enriched (ER–/PR–/HER2+):} 6 dysregulations (25 \%)  
    TP53, PIK3CA, PTEN, ERBB2, MYC, FGFR1; \( \mathrm{NRCI} = 0.7500 \)
  \item \textbf{Triple‑Negative (TNBC):} 10 dysregulations (42 \%)  
    TP53, PIK3CA, PTEN, BRCA1, BRCA2, RB1, MYC, RUNX1, NF1, MAP2K4; \( \mathrm{NRCI} = 0.5833 \)
\end{itemize}

\subsection{Simulation Parameters}

Each molecular subtype was tested across a complete resonance sweep:
\begin{itemize}[leftmargin=1.5em]
  \item Frequency range: 37 frequencies per subtype  
  \item Iterations: 20 per frequency  
  \item Observer intent factor: \( F_{\mu\nu} = 1.5 \) (conscious observation amplification)  
  \item GLR correction: error rate \( a \approx b \) 1 \%, selective targeting applied  
  \item Restoration threshold: \( \mathrm{NRCI} \geq 1.0 \)
\end{itemize}

\subsection{Computational Platform}

All simulations were performed using Python 3.x with NumPy and SciPy libraries, under a fixed random seed of 42 for complete reproducibility.  
The methodological design followed the same statistical and computational alignment used in prior UBP analyses of prostate cancer resonance studies.



